  "id": "COMPOUND:980 - PROTEIN:5387",
  "verbalization": "Doxorubicin is linked to A-427 through a series of molecular interactions involving purinoceptors and other compounds. The evidence suggests that doxorubicin targets P2X purinoceptor 1, which is subsequently targeted by palmarumycin CP18, and this pathway leads to A-427. Similarly, doxorubicin also targets NCI-H1522, which is also targeted by palmarumycin CP18, reinforcing the role of this compound in the pathway. Additionally, doxorubicin is linked to Mollicellin N, which also targets A-427. These findings collectively indicate that doxorubicin exerts its effects through a series of molecular interactions involving purinoceptors and other compounds, ultimately leading to the activation of A-427. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which doxorubicin influences A-427, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
